Paperly must function as a genuinely useful standalone PDF reader, not just a PDF preview attached to the conversion utilities.

## 6.1 File Opening

Support:

- Opening local PDF files.
- Android document picker.
- Opening PDFs from recent documents.
- Android native file-opening intents.
- Opening compatible documents through Android sharing.
- Restoring previously opened documents.
- Remembering the last reading position.

No file uploads or external processing.

## 6.2 Reading Interface

Implement:

- Continuous vertical scrolling.
- Single-page viewing.
- Horizontal page navigation.
- Page thumbnails.
- Page number navigation.
- Pinch-to-zoom.
- Double-tap zoom.
- Fit-to-width.
- Fit-to-page.
- Full-screen reading mode.
- Page rotation.
- Reading-position restoration.

Render pages efficiently.

Do not load an entire large document into memory unnecessarily.

Use lazy rendering or an equivalent efficient document-rendering strategy.

## 6.3 Text Interaction

Provide:

- Text selection.
- Copy selected text.
- Search inside documents.
- Search result navigation.
- Text selection handles.
- Native Android interaction where supported.

Clearly differentiate text-based PDFs from scanned documents.

Do not claim scanned documents contain searchable text when they do not.

Offline OCR can be considered as a separate future feature.

## 6.4 Navigation and Bookmarks

Implement:

- Add bookmarks.
- Remove bookmarks.
- Bookmark navigation.
- Recent reading positions.
- Page thumbnails.
