# 12. PRIVACY AND OFFLINE ARCHITECTURE

This is a strict requirement.

Paperly must operate entirely offline.

The final Android application must not communicate with external servers.

Explicitly prohibit:

- Analytics SDKs.
- Advertising SDKs.
- Tracking libraries.
- Telemetry.
- Crash-report uploads.
- Cloud synchronisation.
- Cloud document processing.
- Accounts.
- Registration.
- Login.
- Remote configuration.
- External APIs.
- Remote theme downloads.
- Remote font downloads.
- Periodic server pings.
- Online licence verification.
- Advertising identifiers.
- Device fingerprinting.
- Google Play Integrity checks.
- SafetyNet checks.

Do not include Android's INTERNET permission in the final merged application manifest.

Audit direct and transitive dependencies.

All fonts, theme assets, icons and required processing libraries must be locally available.

The application must work in airplane mode from first launch through document opening, viewing, processing, exporting and local sharing.

Do not introduce hidden background services or network-dependent fallbacks.

All settings, bookmarks, theme configurations and recent history must be stored locally.

